## 3. Canonical Operator I objects

- Controlled viability: existential policy/trajectory.
- Robust or discriminating viability: one causal policy against all declared disturbances or strategies.
- Fixed-policy safety: all declared disturbances under one fixed policy.
- Epistemic viability: kernel on information/history states under observation-based policies.
- Institutional viability: epistemic/robust kernel after authority, prescription, implementation, enforcement, and compliance restrictions.
- Chance viability: pathwise probability under an explicit law and filtration.
- Recovery: capture basin with target, envelope, horizon, policy class, and disturbance class.

Literal inclusion requires a common state space, safe set, horizon, information pattern, and aligned policy/disturbance classes. Belief-space objects are compared through a prior domain, refinement map, or physical projection.

